+  title: V595 evidence synthesis and branch disposition
+  track: infrastructure
+  priority: critical
+  agent_type: codex
+  model: gpt-5.6-sol
+  requires_gpu: false
+  max_turns: 50
+  estimated_wall_time_min: 180
+  per_unit_rows: true
+  milestone: 2026.08.595
+  deliverable: results/experiment_6823_v595_branch_disposition.json
+  prompt: |
+    CONTEXT:
+    V595 separates contract repair from selective arbitration, verified route memory, and live ARC
+    evidence. Read every terminal artifact, including blocked, disqualified, null, partial, and
+    flagged evidence. This task is deliberately ungated so every branch receives a disposition.
+
+    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
+
+    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
+    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
+    - {project_root}/research-program.md and {project_root}/_bmad/prd.md, FR11 and FR12
+    - {project_root}/openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md
+    - {project_root}/research-roadmap.yaml
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6810_v595_contract_manifest_preflight.json through
+      {project_root}/results/experiment_6822_arc_causal_adoption_audit.json
+    - {project_root}/scripts/adversarial_verify.py
+    - {project_root}/scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py
+
+    TASK:
+    Recompute V595 claims from all terminal rows. Compare the executed manifest with the design.
+    Decide adopt, narrow, retire, or blocked for the selective arbiter, verified route memory, and
+    live ARC path. Do not run an experiment or invoke an LLM.
+
+    CONCRETE STEPS:
+    0. PRECONDITIONS: hash the design, executed roadmap, owned specs, and every expected terminal
+       artifact. Missing, malformed, blocked, disqualified, partial, or flagged artifacts remain
+       explicit rows. They do not block this ungated task. If evidence is incomplete, continue with
+       the closed disposition `blocked` for the affected branch and record gate_check_summary.
+    1. Write tests first for fourteen-task identity, terminal-class preservation, source hashes,
+       row reducers, missing artifacts, flagged evidence, blocked branches, and closed decisions.
+    2. Load Exp6810 through Exp6822 by exact path. Re-run adversarial verification and row-verdict
+       checks. Do not pool a blocked, disqualified, partial, or flagged result into a positive claim.
+    3. Recompute every eligible headline from rows. Keep hard safety, utility, transport, memory
+       causality, portability, and live progress decisions separate.
+    4. Compare the executed manifest with the four design phases, fourteen task IDs, gates,
+       deliverables, models, and owned REQ map. Record all differences.
+    5. Issue adopt, narrow, retire, or blocked for each branch. A positive decision requires its
+       independent cold audit. A clean null narrows or retires. A resource block stays blocked.
+    6. Emit one row per task and one row per branch. This task writes no new scientific claim and
+       invokes no experiment implementation.
+    7. Run focused tests, ruff, OpenSpec coverage, prior-failure validation, gate-contract audit,
+       artifact convention audit, adversarial verification, and root-clutter checks.
+    8. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS AND PRINCIPLES: field_principles (principle per field);
+       inference_substrate (CPU aggregation from upstream artifacts, no LLM); duration_s (measured
+       wall time); random_seed (fixed audit seed); reproducibility_checksum (bind inputs, rows,
+       commands, and output); source_artifact_hashes (all terminal evidence); roadmap_identity
+       (exact milestone and task range); contract_owner_map (existing spec and REQ per contract);
+       rows (one task or branch decision per row); task_count (must be fourteen);
+       terminal_class_counts (preserve every result class); gate_check_summary (failed check,
+       expected value, and observed value); adversarial_findings (flagged evidence stays excluded);
+       row_recomputed_claims (eligible evidence only); manifest_comparison (design versus execution);
+       selective_arbiter_disposition (closed decision); verified_route_memory_disposition (closed
+       decision); live_arc_disposition (closed decision); disposition_enum (adopt | narrow | retire
+       | blocked); solve_claim (false); verifier_is_oracle (false, this synthesis does not define
+       correctness); verdict_class (closed enum: positive | circular_positive | null | blocked |
+       disqualified | partial); honest_verdict (terminal and evidence-bounded).
+
+    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6823_v595_branch_disposition.py --date {date}
+    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
+  prior_failures:
+    - experiment_id: exp6780-v590-branch-disposition
+      verdict: 'complete_partial: branch evidence remained blocked or missing and the artifact was flagged'
+      addressed_by: 'This disposition is ungated, preserves every terminal class, excludes flagged evidence from positive claims, and compares the full fourteen-task executed manifest with the design.'
+      retire_if_same_verdict: true
